 \section{Introduction}  
 The field of dialogue systems has seen rapid development in recent years, with a focus on creating models that can engage in open-domain conversation.  These systems are designed to interact naturally with people across a wide range of topics.  Various approaches have been developed to enhance their performance.  For instance, encoder-decoder frameworks and generative adversarial networks have been proposed.  Although these approaches have demonstrated effectiveness, they tend to overlook incorporating relevant context from a trained corpus.  
